{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791296591177,"sessionID":"ses_eee675193ffeOYa3FO37uP0Phw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a11198d38572debe77065c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/dsflash-max__routing__r1__1791296580/work/answers.json","content":"[\n  {\"id\": \"q1\", \"model\": \"atlas-pro\", \"effort\": \"high\"},\n  {\"id\": \"q2\", \"model\": \"atlas-pro\", \"effort\": \"high\"},\n  {\"id\": \"q3\", \"model\": \"Unrouted\", \"effort\": null},\n  {\"id\": \"q4\", \"model\": \"atlas-lite\", \"effort\": \"high\"},\n  {\"id\": \"q5\", \"model\": \"corvid-mini\", \"effort\": \"medium\"},\n  {\"id\": \"q6\", \"model\": \"pellet-2\", \"effort\": \"high\"}\n]\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/dsflash-max__routing__r1__1791296580/work/answers.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/dsflash-max__routing__r1__1791296580/work/answers.json","time":{"start":1791296591163,"end":1791296591168}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me work through each request carefully.\n\nPolicy:\n- Effort scale: low < medium < high < max.\n- Models table:\n  - atlas-pro: Northwind, nw, lanes: implement, review, research; floor high, ceiling max.\n  - atlas-lite: Northwind, nw, lanes: extract, prose; floor low, ceiling high.\n  - corvid-9: Corvid, cv, lanes: implement, review; floor medium, ceiling max.\n  - corvid-mini: Corvid, cv, lanes: extract; floor low, ceiling medium.\n  - pellet-2: Pellet, pl, lanes: prose, research; floor medium, ceiling high.\n- Lane order (first eligible wins):\n  - implement: atlas-pro, corvid-9\n  - review: corvid-9, atlas-pro\n  - research: atlas-pro, pellet-2\n  - extract: corvid-mini, atlas-lite\n  - prose: pellet-2, atlas-lite\n- R1: eligibility requires lane in lanes column.\n- R2: review lane: model's family must differ from request's author_family.\n- R3: pinned cli → only models on that cli eligible.\n- R4: skip unavailable models.\n- R5: if none eligible → Unrouted, effort null.\n- R6: effort adjustment: below floor → floor; above ceiling → ceiling; else keep. Effort never makes a model ineligible.\n\nNow each request:\n\nq1: implement, effort medium.\n- implement order: atlas-pro (lanes include implement, no constraints) → eligible. atlas-pro floor high, ceiling max. Requested medium < high → use high.\n- Answer: model atlas-pro, effort high.\n\nq2: review, effort high, author_family Corvid.\n- review order: corvid-9 first. R2: model family Corvid must differ from author_family Corvid → corvid-9 family Corvid = author family Corvid → not eligible.\n- Next atlas-pro: family Northwind ≠ Corvid → eligible. floor high, ceiling max. Requested high is within [high, max] → keep high.\n- Answer: atlas-pro, high.\n\nq3: extract, effort low, pinned_cli \"pl\".\n- extract order: corvid-mini (cv) — pinned cli pl → not eligible. atlas-lite (nw) — not eligible. No models on pl in extract lane... pellet-2 is pl but lanes prose, research; R1 fails. So no eligible → Unrouted, effort null.\n- Answer: Unrouted, null.\n\nq4: prose, effort max, unavailable [\"pellet-2\"].\n- prose order: pellet-2 unavailable → skip. atlas-lite: lanes prose, eligible. Floor low, ceiling high. Requested max > ceiling high → use high.\n- Answer: atlas-lite, high.\n\nq5: extract, effort max.\n- extract order: corvid-mini first: lanes extract, eligible. Floor low, ceiling medium. Requested max > medium → medium.\n- Answer: corvid-mini, medium.\n\nq6: research, effort high, pinned_cli \"pl\".\n- research order: atlas-pro (nw) — pinned pl → not eligible. pellet-2 (pl) — eligible. Floor medium, ceiling high. Requested high within → high.\n- Answer: pellet-2, high.\n\nWrite answers.json exactly:\n[{\"id\": \"q1\", \"model\": \"atlas-pro\", \"effort\": \"high\"}, ...]\n\nThe format specified: answers.json = [{\"id\": \"...\", \"model\": \"...\", \"effort\": \"...\" or null}, ...]. One object per request in order.\n\nLet me write the file. Working directory is the scratchpad work dir.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_11198d389001Ns2DBAGLNb2hR1","sessionID":"ses_eee675193ffeOYa3FO37uP0Phw","messageID":"msg_11198cad1001Vb3YbM93GjMMx8"}}
